  "articleBody": "Installing bathroom safety rails incorrectly can actually make your bathroom less safe, which is the exact opposite of what you want! One of the most frequent mistakes is placing the bars where they can't be reached during a transfer. You need to think about your actual movement patterns in the shower or tub. Another big one is mounting them without proper structural support. Just drilling into drywall or even some tile isn't enough; you need to hit those studs or have solid blocking behind the wall. And please, don't rely on those suction-cup devices for real support—they just aren't designed for load-bearing and can come loose. People also often fail to account for wet hands, soap residue, or nearby obstructions that might make gripping difficult. The bar needs to be easy to grab in real-world, slippery conditions. If you're dealing with hollow walls, tile, or just want to be absolutely sure everything is secure and perfectly placed for your needs, calling in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC is a smart move. We can ensure a safe and effective installation every time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}